# Force LF line endings for files that run inside Linux containers or shells,
# regardless of the checkout platform's core.autocrlf setting. Without this,
# a Windows checkout can silently convert shebang scripts to CRLF, which
# breaks `exec` in the container with "no such file or directory" (the
# kernel looks for an interpreter literally named e.g. "/bin/sh\r").
*.sh      text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf
